Week–2: Single-Node Kafka Operations

Aim: To create a Kafka topic and perform basic producer and consumer operations.

1. Start Kafka
docker run -d --name zookeeper -p 2181:2181 wurstmeister/zookeeper

docker run -d --name kafka -p 9092:9092 --link zookeeper:zookeeper \
-e KAFKA_ZOOKEEPER_CONNECT=zookeeper:2181 \
-e KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS=PLAINTEXT://localhost:9092 \
-e KAFKA_LISTENERS=PLAINTEXT://0.0.0.0:9092 \
wurstmeister/kafka
2. Create Topic
bin/kafka-topics.sh --create --topic test-topic \
--bootstrap-server localhost:9092
3. Produce Messages
bin/kafka-console-producer.sh --topic test-topic \
--bootstrap-server localhost:9092

Enter:

Hello
Kafka Test
4. Consume Messages

Open another terminal:

bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh --topic test-topic \
--from-beginning --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

Output:

Hello
Kafka Test
Result

Thus, Kafka topic was created and messages were successfully produced and consumed.
